oracle_direction_summary:
CCodePrinter in sympy/printing/ccode.py gains _print_sinc, which rewrites sinc(x) as Piecewise((sin(x)/x, Ne(x, 0)), (1, True)) and prints it, and _print_Relational, which emits C comparison operators. ccode(sinc(x)) therefore returns ((x != 0) ? (
   sin(x)/x
)
: (
   1
)) instead of the 'Not supported in C' comment, and test_ccode_Relational pins ccode(Eq(x, y)) == 'x == y' and its five siblings.
